# FFI handlers

Follow the project skill `.agents/skills/add-ffi-handler/SKILL.md`.

- `dispatch.go` only routes to `api/ffi/handlers`: add the `case` in `route`. `Call` recovers a panic into `internal.unknown`, so handlers never `recover`. New RPCs get a handler file and `runRPC` table tests, not a `run` closure in the table.
- Failed `provenencia_call` returns protobuf `Error` in `out` (status 1), not UTF-8 English. Domain errors use `core/apperr` codes.
- Catalog SQLite RPCs use `withProjectCatalog` / `catalogsession` — see `.agents/skills/use-catalog-session/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/rules/catalog-session.mdc`.
